# Prefer `switch` over chained `if`

When matching a value against a closed set of constants, use `switch`, not
`if` / `else if` or a `||` equality chain. Keep `if` for ranges and compound
predicates. Skip vendored `M5*` / `ft8_lib`.

See `docs/STYLE.md`.
